  "headline": "Spironolactone is not on FDA's shortage list; Corvale East has 8.5 days of 100 mg tablets and Corvale General has 27 days, so a transfer of 69 tablets is the top option",
  "headline_cites": ["D6", "D1", "D2", "D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows spironolactone is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 106 tablets of the 100 mg strength at 12.5 tablets per day, giving 8.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 375 tablets of the same strength at 13.9 tablets per day, giving 27 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option 1 is to transfer 69 tablets of 100 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale General with 22 days and bring Corvale East to 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Both sites' 100 mg product carries NDC 70518372103 and is labeled by REMEDYREPACK INC., whose label names OXFORD PHARMS as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E3", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternate manufacturer option is Accord Healthcare, Inc., which is also not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Another alternate is Advagen Pharma Ltd., likewise not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    }
  ]
}
